== ConvoWizard privacy disclosure ==

ConvoWizard is an optional (opt-in) gadget for talk-page drafting feedback. When enabled, it sends limited discussion data to a Cornell-hosted backend for scoring before a reply is posted.

=== Data sent by the gadget ===
* Username (`wgUserName`).
* Page URL where the reply is being drafted.
* Extracted discussion context text from the current thread.
* Draft reply text while the user is typing.
* Interaction and token identifiers required by the service.

=== Data retained by the backend ===
* Action log records (including text payload): retained until manual deletion by maintainers.
* Token metadata: retained until manual deletion by maintainers.
* Infrastructure/server logs (for example IP and user-agent, where collected by hosting/proxy): retained per host defaults, currently up to 30 days.

=== Deletion requests ===
To request deletion of ConvoWizard records, contact: `hr328@cornell.edu`.

Please include:
* Wikipedia username.
* Approximate date/time (UTC) of activity.
* Link(s) to affected talk page(s), if available.

Deletion requests are acknowledged as soon as practical and processed within 30 days.

=== User control ===
* ConvoWizard is opt-in (not enabled by default).
* Users can disable it at any time in Preferences.
* Invalid tokens are automatically cleared by gadget logic.
